1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,528
An outbound calling campaign takes a list of contacts and has agents call

2
00:00:05,528 --> 00:00:08,680
them, with every call checked against your rules.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:12,864
This video follows the whole story, from the features to turn on to

4
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:14,469
what each person does.

5
00:00:14,469 --> 00:00:18,710
Calls never connect on this demo site, so the live parts use slides.

6
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:27,565
This is for managers who run calling campaigns, such as a lead drive,

7
00:00:27,565 --> 00:00:32,670
renewals or appointment reminders, and for the agents and supervisors who work them.

8
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:37,924
When it is done, your contacts are loaded as call activities for one

9
00:00:37,924 --> 00:00:40,420
campaign, and agents sign in to it.

10
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:46,020
The dialer offers each record in Preview, or places the call in Power and Progressive.

11
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:50,092
Every call passes your compliance checks first:

12
00:00:50,092 --> 00:00:54,166
opt-outs, registries, your calling window and dead numbers.

13
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:59,807
Agents record an outcome, the subject flow schedules the follow-up, and reports show

14
00:00:59,807 --> 00:01:01,750
how far the campaign got.

15
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:09,982
Your administrator turns on the features in Tools, Features.

16
00:01:09,982 --> 00:01:12,425
Omnichannel Management is the base.

17
00:01:12,425 --> 00:01:18,144
Contact Center Outbound Dialer gives you Preview dialing, and Contact Center Paced Dialing

18
00:01:18,144 --> 00:01:20,110
adds Power and Progressive.

19
00:01:20,110 --> 00:01:22,612
Agents also need Agent Entitlements.

20
00:01:22,612 --> 00:01:27,498
Managers need the permissions for the setup pages, and agents need the Agent

21
00:01:27,498 --> 00:01:30,000
role with the soft phone permission.

22
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,828
Start with the data and the outcomes.

23
00:01:36,828 --> 00:01:42,327
Import your contacts, create the subject, create the dispositions, and add an action

24
00:01:42,327 --> 00:01:45,260
to the subject flow for every one of them.

25
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:47,652
Then set the rules.

26
00:01:47,652 --> 00:01:54,220
Create the campaign, a business hours calendar for the calling window, and the dialer profile.

27
00:01:54,970 --> 00:01:56,393
Then the people.

28
00:01:56,393 --> 00:02:00,080
Add the campaign to the entitlements of each agent.

29
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:04,840
Last, load the work, and let agents dial.

30
00:02:09,046 --> 00:02:10,574
Create the subject.

31
00:02:10,574 --> 00:02:15,220
On Subject Flows, click Create a new content type, name it Spring lead

32
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,054
drive, and click Create.

33
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:21,578
Then find the Omnichannel Subject part, and click Add and Configure.

34
00:02:21,578 --> 00:02:26,346
The fields you add to a subject are what agents fill in during the call.

35
00:02:26,829 --> 00:02:31,177
The part settings pick a Default campaign, here Spring lead drive.

36
00:02:31,177 --> 00:02:34,075
Direction is Outbound, for work you start.

37
00:02:34,075 --> 00:02:36,914
Inbound is for customers who contact you.

38
00:02:36,914 --> 00:02:42,470
Require a disposition stays on, because the disposition is what runs the subject flow.

39
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,799
Then click Save.

40
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:47,480
The subject now appears on Subject Flows.

41
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,226
Click Manage Flow, then Add Action.

42
00:02:50,226 --> 00:02:55,853
Finish ends the task, Try Again calls later, New Activity creates a follow-up,

43
00:02:55,853 --> 00:02:59,270
and Convert Lead turns a lead into a contact.

44
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:01,681
Add one for every disposition.

45
00:03:05,966 --> 00:03:11,555
The dispositions are the outcomes agents can pick, such as Call Back Later and Not Interested.

46
00:03:11,555 --> 00:03:16,306
One has the Number not in service outcome, so dead numbers are handled for you.

47
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:21,101
The campaign is what agents sign in to, and a business hours calendar

48
00:03:21,101 --> 00:03:25,460
sets the hours you may call, checked in the time zone of each contact.

49
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:29,583
The dialer profile chooses how to dial:

50
00:03:29,583 --> 00:03:35,860
the mode, the caller ID, the compliance rules with your calling calendar, and the retry settings.

51
00:03:36,351 --> 00:03:41,804
On the entitlements of each agent, add the campaign under Allowed campaigns.

52
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:47,391
Without the Agent Entitlements feature, any agent may sign in to any campaign.

53
00:03:51,635 --> 00:03:55,289
Open Load Activities, and click Add Activity Load.

54
00:03:55,289 --> 00:03:58,618
The sources are Automatic, Dialer and Manual.

55
00:03:58,618 --> 00:04:04,295
Dialer activities stay unassigned until the dialer reserves them for an agent, so

56
00:04:04,295 --> 00:04:06,775
a campaign of calls uses Dialer.

57
00:04:07,252 --> 00:04:13,139
Enter a Title, then pick the Subject content type, the Campaign and the Dialer profile.

58
00:04:13,139 --> 00:04:17,507
The campaign is required, unless the subject has a default one.

59
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:19,280
Dial from is optional:

60
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:23,522
pick a number if this campaign should show its own caller ID.

61
00:04:25,097 --> 00:04:29,530
Pick the Record type, contacts or leads, and filter who is loaded.

62
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:35,011
Prevent duplicate activity with the same subject keeps contacts who already have an

63
00:04:35,011 --> 00:04:37,597
open activity out of the load twice.

64
00:04:37,597 --> 00:04:39,137
Then save the load.

65
00:04:40,423 --> 00:04:43,322
Choose Load activities from the Actions menu.

66
00:04:43,322 --> 00:04:47,641
When it finishes, the list shows that it loaded two of three contacts,

67
00:04:47,641 --> 00:04:52,473
and skipped one, because its only number is on the Numbers Not In Service list.

68
00:04:56,673 --> 00:05:00,297
Agents sign in to the campaign from the Work tab of the soft

69
00:05:00,297 --> 00:05:02,603
phone, and set themselves Available.

70
00:05:03,353 --> 00:05:07,348
With Preview, each record is offered with Dial and Skip.

71
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:13,793
The agent reviews it, clicks Dial, and the server places the call after the compliance checks.

72
00:05:14,543 --> 00:05:19,450
With Power or Progressive, the dialer places the call for an available agent,

73
00:05:19,450 --> 00:05:22,583
and the record opens when the customer answers.

74
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:28,635
After the call, the agent completes the activity with a disposition and notes.

75
00:05:28,635 --> 00:05:31,854
That ends wrap-up, and runs the subject flow:

76
00:05:31,854 --> 00:05:34,253
try again later, or a follow-up.

77
00:05:38,553 --> 00:05:43,432
Supervisors watch the live dashboard, which can be filtered by the campaign.

78
00:05:43,432 --> 00:05:47,895
It lists the queues and the agents, and under Why isn't this dialing,

79
00:05:47,895 --> 00:05:49,859
what holds a campaign back.

80
00:05:49,859 --> 00:05:53,787
It is empty here, because no agent is signed in, and no call

81
00:05:53,787 --> 00:05:55,453
connects on this site.

82
00:05:55,953 --> 00:06:02,805
Managers use Manage Activities to reassign, reschedule or move work to another dialer profile in bulk.

83
00:06:02,805 --> 00:06:06,993
They also review the dead numbers on Numbers Not In Service.

84
00:06:11,193 --> 00:06:15,269
To check that it works, load a small list, sign in as a

85
00:06:15,269 --> 00:06:17,608
test agent, and be Available.

86
00:06:17,608 --> 00:06:20,749
With Preview, an offer appears with Dial.

87
00:06:20,749 --> 00:06:23,623
With Power, a call is placed at once.

88
00:06:24,373 --> 00:06:30,514
Complete the test activity with Call back, and check that the flow scheduled the next attempt.

89
00:06:30,514 --> 00:06:32,725
Then run the Campaign summary.

90
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:39,113
Subject inventory, Disposition breakdown, Agent productivity and Dialer call detail show the rest.

91
00:06:41,113 --> 00:06:45,419
Set up the data, the outcomes and the rules once, load a list,

92
00:06:45,419 --> 00:06:50,486
and agents dial it, with every call checked and every outcome followed up.

93
00:06:50,486 --> 00:06:52,133
Thanks for watching.

